 "note": "The press-two-tabs latch, v7, battery side: v6 run through four tests (error tolerance at every swap step, centred forces, the parts on hand, stressed parts as big as fits) and changed where it failed. Cut at the tab line. The XT60 is 42.8 mm from the pull, so the two nubs carry 170.5 N, not 59: nubs 13 wide, feet 18 wide, blades 4.7 x 16 (worst index 0.723). 15 deg wedge: +-0.21 mm of height tolerance (v6 +-0.14). The blade pushes one crowned pad on the slider's centre line. A steel pin inside each spring. Receiver, XT60 carrier, guide poles, bolts and their steel pins are v5's. Numbers under the viewer.",
